<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Quantitative evaluation of cropping strategy.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.5.1 Ablation on Cropping Strategy ‣ 4.5 Ablation study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ AdaFocus: Knowing When and Where to Look for Adaptive Visual Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 2</span></a>, our adaptive cropping strategy consistently improves accuracy compared to indiscriminate cropping (<span id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w/o cropping strategy</span>). For Qwen2.5-VL, our strategy yields a +1.14% boost on AOKVQA and +0.52% on V*-Bench. This confirms that indiscriminate cropping introduces visual noise and misjudgments, which our selective strategy effectively avoids.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
